# Glossary term pages (featdd/dpn-glossary) render on the glossary listing
# page, so they inherit its description: every term page carried the same
# "n terms from ..." text. dpn-glossary only sets the term's own
# meta_description, which is rarely maintained, and EXT:seo adds the listing
# page's description from the page record. Without `replace` a value set here
# never reaches the tag. It now carries the term's meta description, else its
# definition, else its tooltip (GlossaryTermService::describeTerm), and
# og:description follows it.
#
# The routing argument is the uid of the default-language term; the service
# reads the record in the page language.
#
# Null-safe on purpose: the frontend TypoScript is also built in backend
# requests (a backend module that renders a page's TypoScript), and those carry
# no page arguments. `request.getPageArguments().getArguments()` then aborted
# the whole module with "Unable to call method getArguments of non-object"
# (500 in the page module of the pilot site, 2026-10-02).
[traverse(request.getPageArguments()?.getArguments() ?? [], 'tx_dpnglossary_glossary/term') != '']
    page.meta.description >
    page.meta.description {
        cObject = USER
        cObject {
            userFunc = Koh\StructuredContent\Presentation\UserFunction\GlossaryTermMetaDescription->render
            maxLength = 155
        }
        replace = 1
    }
    page.meta.og:description < page.meta.description
    page.meta.og:description.attribute = property
[END]
